  "note": "Triennial election of the whole council (fifteen seats, one area), polled 15 January 1902; counting began at 9.20 p.m. and the returning officer, Wm. Wilson, announced the poll at 11.45: \"The first fifteen were declared elected.\" Eighteen candidates. Party labels are not printed. Dr Liddle's forename is not given. Clement Courtney: no party label printed in 1902. At other elections he stood as Unionist (Portadown, 16 January 1899, listed as Unionist: Belfast News-Letter, 18 January 1899, p. 7 (\"Urban District Councils\"); the editorial in the Portadown News, 21 January 1899, p. 4). Charles Johnston: no party label printed in 1902. At other elections he stood as Unionist (Portadown, Armagh County Council, 6 April 1899, printed 'U': Lurgan Mail, 15 April 1899, p. 6 (\"Election Results: Armagh Co. Council Returns\"); party labels from the Northern Star, 15 April 1899, p. 5, and the Portadown News, 15 April 1899, p. 8; figures checked against those two and the Portadown News, 8 April 1899, p. 5; Portadown, Armagh County Council, 28 May 1902, printed 'U': Lurgan Mail, 10 May 1902, p. 5 (\"The Elections: Armagh County Council\"); labels from the Armagh Guardian, 2 May 1902, p. 2 (\"But Few Contests\": county council nominations, with labels)). W. G. Hewitt: no party label printed in 1902. At other elections he stood as Unionist (Portadown, 16 January 1899, listed as Unionist: Belfast News-Letter, 18 January 1899, p. 7 (\"Urban District Councils\"); the editorial in the Portadown News, 21 January 1899, p. 4). W. J. Johnston: no party label printed in 1902. At other elections he stood as Unionist (Portadown, 16 January 1899, listed as Unionist: Belfast News-Letter, 18 January 1899, p. 7 (\"Urban District Councils\"); the editorial in the Portadown News, 21 January 1899, p. 4). His labels elsewhere differ (UUP x3, Town Tenants' Association x1). John Davison: no party label printed in 1902. At other elections he stood as Unionist (Portadown, 16 January 1899, listed as Unionist: Belfast News-Letter, 18 January 1899, p. 7 (\"Urban District Councils\"); the editorial in the Portadown News, 21 January 1899, p. 4)."
}
